[statement]
As `a-package-losing-a-name-it-provides-is-removed-at-the-turn-of-its-successor`,
with the name taken the package's own: `bar`, which the request brings,
provides `foo` at a version, and apk removes the installed `foo` just
before installing `bar`, after `a` and `b`.

[repository]
P:foo
V:1

P:bar
V:1
p:foo=2

P:app
V:1
D:a b bar

P:a
V:1

P:b
V:1

[installed]
P:old
V:1

P:foo
V:1

[world]
old

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install a 1
install b 1
remove foo 1
install bar 1
install app 1
